"Replace the single queued_action_state slot with an ordered queue component (entries: Vec<QueuedAction{action_id, target_entity_id, automatic}>). Rule: at most ONE manual entry at a time (a new manual enqueue replaces the manual entry, never the automatics); AUTOMATIC entries (system-forced re-arm) are flagged, skip that cap, and insert at the FRONT - so a forced re-arm never clobbers the player's queued intent. All queue mutations flow through fixed enqueue/shift methods that dirty the action-queue flag (validation stays change-driven). Shift pops the front; the interruptible rule is unchanged. Client: isQueued reads the queue; turn guard and actionless stamping count any entry."